# agy acp, Antigravity CLI 1.5.14 (linux x64), probed on adacachy on 2026-11-21 by kiln agent
# 01a2007b1b517fcabbf949867c38e4b2 ("Antigravity CLI Support"), with no Google account signed in. Each probe
# piped JSON-RPC lines into `agy acp` (`~/.local/bin/agy`, Google's installer's) and kept its stdout; the
# requests are as sent (a folder's path left out), the answers as agy wrote them. Kept for docs/agents.md and
# gaps.json's antigravity row.

## initialize, with fs and terminal capabilities
> {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"initialize","params":{"protocolVersion":1,"clientCapabilities":{"fs":{"readTextFile":true,"writeTextFile":true},"terminal":true,"_meta":{"terminal-auth":true}}}}
< {"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":{"protocolVersion":1,"agentCapabilities":{"loadSession":true,"load_session":true,"promptCapabilities":{"image":true,"audio":false,"embeddedContext":true},"sessionCapabilities":{"resume":{},"close":{},"load":{},"list":{},"additionalDirectories":{}},"session_capabilities":{"resume":{},"close":{},"load":{},"list":{},"additionalDirectories":{}},"auth":{"logout":{}},"_meta":{"antigravity":{"tier":true,"systemPrompt":{"append":true}}}},"agentInfo":{"name":"Antigravity ACP Server","version":"1.5.14"},"authMethods":[{"id":"oauth-personal","name":"Log in with Google","description":"Log in with your Google account"},{"id":"oauth-business","name":"Log in with Gemini Enterprise","description":"Log in with your Gemini Enterprise account"},{"id":"gemini-api-key","name":"Gemini API key","description":"Use an API key with Gemini Developer API"},{"id":"agent-platform","name":"Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform","description":"Use Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform (formerly Vertex AI) with Application Default Credentials"}]},"id":1}

## session/new with no sign-in (after an initialize without fs or terminal)
> {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"method":"session/new","params":{"cwd":"<a folder>","mcpServers":[]}}
< {"jsonrpc":"2.0","error":{"code":-32000,"message":"Authentication required"},"id":2}

## logout, and two methods it doesn't have (after initialize)
> {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"method":"logout","params":{}}
> {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":3,"method":"auth/logout","params":{}}
> {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":4,"method":"nonexistent/method","params":{}}
< {"jsonrpc":"2.0","error":{"code":-32601,"message":"Method not found: auth/logout"},"id":3}
< {"jsonrpc":"2.0","error":{"code":-32601,"message":"Method not found: nonexistent/method"},"id":4}
< {"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":{},"id":2}

## authenticate with gemini-api-key, GEMINI_API_KEY set to a placeholder in its environment, then session/new
> {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"method":"authenticate","params":{"methodId":"gemini-api-key"}}
> {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":3,"method":"session/new","params":{"cwd":"<a folder>","mcpServers":[]}}
